t_Salt_Pond%2C_St_Maarten.jpg/960px-Great_Salt_Pond%2C_St_Maarten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fresh Pond, Sint Maarten","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.032222,"lo":-63.058889,"d":1956,"ds":"Fresh Pond is a 14 ha water body in Sint Maarten on the island of Saint Martin. It has been identified as an Important Bird Area by BirdLife International because it supports populations of various threatened or restricted-range bird species. Some 2.5 km long by 1 km across, it lies within the capital city of Philipsburg.","wpu":"Fresh Pond, Sint Maarten","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Caribbean_coot.jpg/960px-Caribbean_coot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pelikan Rock, Sint Maarten","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.017778,"lo":-63.018056,"d":3166,"ds":"Pelikan Rock is a small rocky islet, about 1 hectare (2.5 acres) in area, lying to the south-east of the coast of the island of Saint Martin, and belonging to the country of Sint Maarten in the Dutch Caribbean.","wpu":"Pelikan Rock, Sint Maarten","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Brown_pelican_in_flight_%28Bodega_Bay%29.jpg/960px-Brown_pelican_in_flight_%28Bodega_Bay%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lower Prince's Quarter","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.052778,"lo":-63.0425,"d":3910,"ds":"Lower Prince's Quarter is a town in Sint Maarten, in the Kingdom of the Netherlands. It has a population of 8,143 making it the largest settlement on the island of Saint Martin.","wpu":"Lower Prince's Quarter","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Unnamed2_-_panoramio_%281239%29.jpg/960px-Unnamed2_-_panoramio_%281239%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Saint Martin (island)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.06,"lo":-63.05,"d":4674,"ds":"Saint Martin is an island in Leeward Islands of the Lesser Antilles in the northeastern Caribbean, approximately 300 km (190 mi) east of Puerto Rico (United States). The 87 km2 (34 mi2) island has been divided since 1648 roughly 60:40 between France (53 km2 or 20 mi2) and the Kingdom of the Netherlands (34 km2 or 13 mi2), but the Dutch part is more populated than the French.","wpu":"Saint Martin (island)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Saint_Martin_map.svg/960px-Saint_Martin_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Concordia, Saint Martin","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.06,"lo":-63.078056,"d":5648,"ds":"Concordia is a small town on the French side of the island of Saint Martin in the Caribbean. It lies directly to the south of the French side's capital Marigot. The town has a population of 5,639 residents, as of 2016, making it the third most-populous town on the French side, behind Marigot and Grand Case.","wpu":"Concordia, Saint Martin","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/View_of_Concordia_from_Fort_St._Louis%2C_Saint_Martin.jpg/960px-View_of_Concordia_from_Fort_St._Louis%2C_Saint_Martin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mary Star of the Sea Church, Simpson Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.0387,"lo":-63.0973,"d":5698,"ds":"The Mary Star of the Sea Church (Dutch: Maria Sterre der Zee kerk) is a religious building of the Catholic Church located in the town of Simpson Bay in St. Maarten in the Dutch part of the Caribbean island of St. Martin in the Lesser Antilles, a constituent country of the Kingdom of the Netherlands.","wpu":"Mary Star of the Sea Church, Simpson Bay","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Mary_Star_of_the_Sea_Church%2C_Simpson_Bay.jpg/960px-Mary_Star_of_the_Sea_Church%2C_Simpson_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Quartier-d'Orleans","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.071667,"lo":-63.032778,"d":6180,"ds":"Quartier-d'Orléans (French pronunciation: [kaʁtje dɔʁleɑ̃], lit. 'Quarter of Orleans') is a seaside village on the eastern coast of the island of Saint Martin, on the French side of the Antilles.","wpu":"Quartier-d'Orleans","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Rue_de_Round_de_Pond%2C_Quartier_D%27Orl%C3%A9ans%2C_Collectivity_of_Saint_Martin_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Rue_de_Round_de_Pond%2C_Quartier_D%27Orl%C3%A9ans%2C_Collectivity_of_Saint_Martin_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Martin of Tours' Church, Marigot","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.0693,"lo":-63.0841,"d":6863,"ds":"St. Martin of Tours Church (French: Église de Saint Martin de Tours) is a Roman Catholic parish of the Diocese of Basse-Terre located on rue du Fort Louis in the city of Marigot, St. Martin in the Lesser Antilles.","wpu":"St. Martin of Tours' Church, Marigot","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Eglise_Catholique_de_Marigot_%286546099035%29.jpg/960px-Eglise_Catholique_de_Marigot_%286546099035%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sandy Ground, Saint Martin","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.058889,"lo":-63.096944,"d":6888,"ds":"Sandy Ground (French: Sol Sableux) is a coastal community on the French side of the Caribbean island of Saint Martin/Sint Maarten. Sandy Ground is known for its luxury hotels, nature, and beaches.","wpu":"Sandy Ground, Saint Martin","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Sandy_Ground%2C_Saint_Martin.jpg/960px-Sandy_Ground%2C_Saint_Martin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fort Louis (Saint Martin)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.070774,"lo":-63.085404,"d":7076,"ds":"Fort Louis (or Fort St. Louis) is a historic French military fort on the Caribbean island of Saint Martin. It is located in Marigot, the capital of the French side of the island, overlooking Marigot Bay.","wpu":"Fort Louis (Saint Martin)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Fort_St._Louis_over_Marigot%2C_St._Martin_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Fort_St._Louis_over_Marigot%2C_St._Martin_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Simpson Bay Lagoon","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.052,"lo":-63.109,"d":7476,"ds":"Simpson Bay Lagoon (also spelt Simson Bay Lagoon, or referred to simply as the Great Pond) is one of the largest inland lagoons in the West Indies of the Caribbean. It is located on the island of Saint Martin. The border between the French and Dutch halves of the island runs across the centre of the lagoon.","wpu":"Simpson Bay Lagoon","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/St._Martin_-_Grand_%C3%8Elet_and_Fort_%288963744532%29.jpg/960px-St._Martin_-_Grand_%C3%8Elet_and_Fort_%288963744532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sunset Bar and Grill","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.03842,"lo":-63.120273,"d":7972,"ds":"The Sunset Bar and Grill is a small bar located on Maho Beach in Sint Maarten, formerly known as the Sunset Beach Bar. It is best known for its proximity to Princess Juliana International Airport, making it a popular hangout for plane spotters.","wpu":"Sunset Bar and Grill","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Maho_Beach_%288248631789%29.jpg/960px-Maho_Beach_%288248631789%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Maho Beach","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.03983,"lo":-63.12069,"d":8060,"ds":"Maho Beach is a beach on the Dutch side of the Caribbean island of Saint Martin, in the territory of Sint Maarten. It is famous for being adjacent to the Princess Juliana International Airport and is a popular site for tourists and plane watchers, who visit the beach to watch aircraft on final approach land at the airport right at the edge of the water.","wpu":"Maho Beach","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Corsair_Airbus_A330_at_SXM_Bidini.jpg/960px-Corsair_Airbus_A330_at_SXM_Bidini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Orient Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.086944,"lo":-63.021944,"d":8146,"ds":"Orient Bay is a coastal community and beach on the French side of the island of Saint Martin in the Caribbean. It lies on the east coast of the island. Until 1985 the area was undeveloped.","wpu":"Orient Bay","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Orient_Bay%2C_SXM_island_in_the_Caribbean.JPG/960px-Orient_Bay%2C_SXM_island_in_the_Caribbean.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Grand Case","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.101111,"lo":-63.051944,"d":9250,"ds":"Grand Case is a small town on the French side of the island of Saint Martin in the Caribbean. It lies on the Anguilla Channel, on the west coast of the island. Grand Case has a long sandy beach.","wpu":"Grand Case","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Grand_Case_2.jpg/960px-Grand_Case_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mary Star of the Sea Church, Grand Case","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.1011,"lo":-63.0571,"d":9290,"ds":"Mary Star of the Sea Church or Grand Case Catholic Church (French: Église de Marie Etoile de la Mer; Eglise catholique à Grand Case) is a religious building affiliated to the Catholic Church located in Grand Case in the territorial collectivity of Saint Martin, a dependent territory of France that consists of the north half of the island of Saint Martin in the lesser Antilles.","wpu":"Mary Star of the Sea Church, Grand Case","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grand_Case-Catholic_Church-St-Martin-France.jpg/960px-Grand_Case-Catholic_Church-St-Martin-France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Philipsburg (Dutch pronunciation: [ˈfilɪpsˌbʏr(ə)x]) is the main town and capital of Sint Maarten, a constituent country of the Kingdom of the Netherlands. It is located on the southern coast of Saint Martin island, between Great Bay and the Great Salt Pond. It serves as the main port of entry, with the major airport and port located in the vicinity.","wpu":"Philipsburg, Sint Maarten","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/Philipsburg_and_the_Great_Bay%2C_Sint_Maarten%2C_Caribbean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}